hadiths[40]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24380","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, who said: Bilal said: O Messenger of Allah, do not precede me with Amin."
"24381","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiped over the socks and the head-cover."
"24382","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Sa'ib ibn Umar, Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, that Mu'awiyah performed hajj, so he sent to Shaybah ibn Uthman to open the door of the Ka'bah, so he said: Bring Abdullah ibn Umar, so Ibn Umar came, and Mu'awiyah said to him: Has it reached you that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in the Ka'bah, so he said: Yes, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the Ka'bah, and his coming out was delayed, so I found something and went, then I came quickly and found the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, coming out, so I asked Bilal ibn Rabah: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray in the Ka'bah, he said: Yes, he bowed two rak'ahs between the two pillars."
"24383","Waki' narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I said to Bilal: How did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, answer them when they greeted him in prayer, he said: He used to gesture with his hand."
"24384","Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Bilal, who said: He would forbid prayer only at sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of Satan."
"24385","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu al-Ala' narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Yazid, from Abu al-Ala', from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"24386","Yahya ibn Adam and Abu Ahmad said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil al-Muzani, from Bilal, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to announce prayer to him, Abu Ahmad said: While he intended fasting, so he called for a cup and drank and gave me to drink, then went out to the mosque for prayer, and stood praying without ablution, intending the fast."
"24387","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from al-Sunabihi, from Bilal, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Laylat al-Qadr is the night of twenty-four."
"24388","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abd al-Razzaq said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar informed me, Abu Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Abdullah, that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf asking Bilal: How did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wipe over the socks, he said: He relieved himself, then called for a purifier, that is a water-skin, and washed his face and his hands, then wiped over his socks and over the head-cover of the turban, Abd al-Razzaq said: Then he called for a purifier, with the water-skin."
"24389","Hisham ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid informed us, who said: I heard Makhul narrating from Nu'aym ibn Khimarr, from Bilal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wipe over the socks and the head-cover."
"24390","Abu Sa'id, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Makhul narrated to us, from Nu'aym ibn Khimarr, from Bilal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wipe over the socks and the head-cover."
"24391","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the Ka'bah, with Uthman ibn Talhah, Usamah ibn Zayd, and Bilal, and it was locked, then when he came out, I asked Bilal: What did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do, he said: He left two pillars on his right and one pillar on his left and three pillars behind him, then he prayed, and between him and the qiblah were three cubits."
"24392","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil, from Bilal, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to announce prayer to him, while he intended fasting, so he drank then handed to me, and went out to prayer."
"24393","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Makhul informed me, that Nu'aym ibn Khimarr, from Bilal, informed him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wipe over the socks and the head-cover."
"24394","Rawh narrated to us, Uthman ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us, Ibn Umar narrated to me, who said: When the day of the Conquest came, they finished their circumambulation of the House and of al-Safa and al-Marwah, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the House, and Ibn Umar was heedless of him, then when he was told of his entering, he came mounting the necks of the men, and entered following the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, how he prays, and met him at the door coming out, so he asked Bilal the caller to prayer: How did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do when he entered the Ka'bah, he said: He prayed two rak'ahs facing his face, then supplicated Allah, mighty and majestic, a while, then came out."
"24395","Waki' and Muhammad ibn Ja'far said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, Ibn Ja'far said in his hadith: He said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, and Abd al-Razzaq, Sufyan informed us, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiped over the socks and the head-cover."
"24396","Waki' narrated to us, al-Sa'ib ibn Umar narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Bakr, al-Sa'ib ibn Umar informed us, from Abu Mulaykah, from Ibn Umar, who said: I asked Bilal ibn Rabah: Where did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray when he entered the Ka'bah, he said: Between the two pillars, and Ibn Bakr said: Two prostrations."
"24397","Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray when he entered the Ka'bah, he said: Between him and the wall were three cubits."
"24398","Waki' narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated to us, from Shaddad, the freedman of Iyad ibn Amir, from Bilal, that he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to announce prayer to him, and found him taking suhur in the mosque of his house."
"24399","Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ward ibn Thumamah, from Amr ibn Mirdas, who said: I came to Sham once, and there was a man thick of lips, or he said: large of lips and nose, with a weapon before him, and they asked him, while he said: O people, take of this weapon and repair it and strive in the cause of Allah, mighty and majestic, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, I said: Who is this, they said: Bilal."
"24400","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abu Abdullah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, who said: I was sitting with Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, then Bilal passed, so he asked him about wiping over the socks, so he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would relieve his need, so I would bring him water, and he would perform ablution and wipe over the turban and over the socks."
"24401","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-A'mash informed us, from al-Hakam ibn Utbah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from Bilal: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"24402","Marwan ibn Shuja' narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that he asked Bilal, and he informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed two rak'ahs, placing the pillar to his right, moving forward a little, and placing the Maqam behind his back."
"24403","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Ibn Bakr: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from Ibn Umar, that he informed him, from Bilal, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed two rak'ahs in it."
"24404","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sayf ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Mujahid say: Ibn Umar was approached while he was in his house, and it was said to him: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has entered the Ka'bah. He said: So I came forward. He said: And I found the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had come out, and I found Bilal standing between the two doorposts. So I said: O Bilal, did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray inside the Ka'bah? He said: Yes, he performed two rak'ahs between these two pillars, and he pointed to the two pillars that are on your left when you enter. He said: Then he came out and prayed two rak'ahs facing the Ka'bah."
"24405","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Makhul, from Nu'aym ibn Khimar, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wipe over the khuffs and the khimar."
"24406","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Sa'id ibn al-As narrated to us, from Sa'id, meaning his father, who said: Mu'awiyah performed Umrah and entered the House, and he sent for Ibn Umar and sat waiting for him until he came to him. He said: Where did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray on the day he entered the House? He said: I was not with him, but I entered after he intended to leave, and I met Bilal and asked him where he prayed, and he informed me that he prayed between the two pillars. So Mu'awiyah stood and prayed between them."
"24407","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Ala' narrated to us, Abu Ziyad Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad al-Kindi narrated to me, from Bilal, that he narrated to him that he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to announce to him the dawn prayer, but A'ishah kept Bilal busy with a matter she asked him about until the morning exposed him and it became quite late. He said: So Bilal stood and announced the prayer to him, continuing his adhan, but the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not come out. When he came out and prayed with the people, he informed him that A'ishah had kept him busy with a matter she asked him about until it became quite late, and then he was slow in coming out. He said: I performed the two rak'ahs of Fajr. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it has become quite late. He said: Even if it had become later than it has, I would have performed them, and performed them well and beautifully."
"24408","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Khattabi narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, who said: And I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping over the khuffs and the khimar."
"24409","Hasan ibn al-Rabi' and Abu Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Abu Isra'il narrated to us; Abu Ahmad said in his hadith: al-Hakam narrated to us; from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me not to repeat the call in any of the prayers except the Fajr prayer. And Abu Ahmad said in his hadith: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: When you give the adhan, do not repeat the call."
"24410","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Abu Zayd Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me not to repeat the call except in Fajr."
"24411","Abu Qatan narrated to us, he said: A man mentioned to Shu'bah: al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal: So he commanded me to repeat the call in Fajr and forbade me from Isha'. Shu'bah said: By Allah, he did not mention Ibn Abi Layla, and he mentioned nothing but a weak chain. I think Shu'bah said: I used to think he narrated it from Imran ibn Muslim."
"24412","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, they said: Za'idah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara', from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wipe over the khuffs."
"24413","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wipe over the khuffs and over the khimar."
"24414","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Idris, from Bilal, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping over the muqayn and the khimar."
"24415","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, al-Hakam informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wipe over the khuffs and the khimar."
"24416","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, that Ibn Umar narrated, from Bilal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed inside the House. He said: And Ibn Abbas used to say: He did not pray in it, but he proclaimed takbir in its corners."
"24417","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal; Shu'bah said: My father wrote, from Abu Uthman; who said: Bilal said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Do not precede me with Amin."
"24418","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ascended the House, with Bilal behind him. He said: And I was a young man, so I ascended, and Bilal met me. I said: What did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do here? He said: He gestured with his hand, meaning: he prayed two rak'ahs."
"24419","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered on the day of the Conquest, riding the camel of Usamah ibn Zayd. He made it kneel, meaning at the Ka'bah, then he called Uthman ibn Talhah for the key. He went to bring it to him, but his mother refused to give it to him. He said: You shall give it to him, or a sword shall come out of my spine. So she handed it to him, and he opened the door. He entered, with Bilal, Uthman, and Usamah with him, and they closed the door upon them for a while. Ibn Umar said: And I was a strong young man, so I hastened ahead of the people and got ahead of them, and I found Bilal standing at the door. I said: Where did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray? He said: Between the two front pillars. And I forgot to ask him how many he prayed."
